{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016MVXeW2YKX4mRvmV6QFx8k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment results for the \"worst\" tier scenario for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment_plan. Let me identify which experiments are still in \"planned\" status:\n\n1. plan_010 - DCOL component ablation - status: planned (but notes say cancelled due to plan_004 failure)\n2. plan_014 - 13B clean FP16 scale validation (Qwen2.5-14B) - status: RUNNING\n3. plan_015 - Wild-data calibration: C4/FineWeb/RedPajama - status: planned\n\n\n4. plan_018 - Existing detector ordinal baseline: Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT - status: planned\n5. plan_020 - Table 1 bootstrap CIs - status: planned\n6. plan_023 - Theoretical analysis - status: planned\n7. plan_026 - API model recursive chains - status: planned\n\nI should also check if there's a theory_section what_if scenario to include. Let me clarify the request - the user is asking for worst-case scenario results for all experiments marked as \"planned\" or currently \"RUNNING\".\n\nLooking at the active experiments: plan_014 is running the Qwen2.5-14B scale validation, while plan_015, plan_018, plan_020, plan_023, and plan_026 are all planned. For the worst-case tier, I'm considering scenarios where the 14B model shows extremely weak signals with 4-class accuracy below 62% and d1v2 AUC under 0.70, the theory section gets dismissed as post-hoc rationalization, multiple reviewers question the methodological contribution, OLMo exhibits seed bias exceeding 5 percentage points, and the Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT baseline performs better than expected.\n\nNow I'm checking the metric ranges to understand the bounds: 14B 4-class accuracy spans 45-61%, d1v2 AUC ranges from 0.55-0.69, feature overlap with 1B is minimal at 0-2, OLMo seed43 accuracy sits at 70-75%, cross-seed variance reaches 5-8 percentage points, and detector ordinal baseline ranges from 55-68%. The cross-strategy d1v2 reversal would represent a fundamental limitation if it occurs across different approaches.\n\nLooking at the experiment statuses, plan_010 is cancelled, plan_014 is currently running, while plan_015, plan_018, plan_020, plan_023, and plan_026 are all planned but not yet started. There's also a killed detector ordinal baseline experiment and olmo_seed43_001 is still analyzing with empty metrics, which ties back to the seed sensitivity concerns.\n\nFor the worst-case scenarios, plan_014 at 14B scale would show 4-class accuracy in the 45-61% range with d1v2 AUC between 0.55-0.69, indicating an extremely weak depth signal at that scale with minimal feature overlap to the 1B model. Plan_015's wild-data calibration would likely reveal high false positive rates in the worst case based on patterns from completed experiments.\n\nPlan_018 with Binoculars and Fast-DetectGPT ordinal baselines would hit 55-68% accuracy, which would undermine the case for needing a specialized approach. Plan_020's bootstrap confidence intervals would come out wide in the worst case, suggesting instability in the estimates. Plan_023's theoretical analysis could be dismissed as post-hoc without verifiable predictions, and plan_026 might show that the depth signal doesn't actually exist for API models.\n\nI should format all these worst-case predictions in YAML, though I'll focus on the planned experiments rather than the still-analyzing olmo_seed43 run.\n\nNow thinking through what each planned experiment would yield under worst-case assumptions. For plan_014 with Qwen2.5-14B, the larger model capacity means recursive fine-tuning causes less distributional shift—the LoRA adjustments affect a smaller fraction of parameters, so adjacent depth distributions overlap heavily and I'd see around 52% 4-class accuracy with 0.62 AUC on the d1v2 comparison. The top features would likely be completely different from the 1B results, with almost no overlap in the top-4 features. Plan_015 involves wild-data calibration across three reference models, building on the individual model results I already have.\n\nFor plan_018 with Binoculars and Fast-DetectGPT, these detectors might actually capture some ordinal signal since model collapse creates progressively more synthetic-looking text, potentially reaching 60-68% accuracy—only about 15 percentage points below the RF baseline, which would challenge the necessity of the specialized 19-feature approach. Plan_020's bootstrap confidence intervals would likely be wide for weaker cells like topk50, with some overlapping adjacent cells depending on seed sensitivity. For plan_023's theory section, the EDD upper bound derivation may not align cleanly with the empirical results.\n\nThe empirical EDD shows a U-shaped pattern at larger scales rather than the monotonic decay the theory predicts, and the strategy-dependent convergence rate argument feels hand-wavy—reviewers will probably see it as retrospective rationalization. Plan_026 with API model fine-tuning risks producing even weaker signals, or the prompted recursive chains might not generate meaningful depth variation. I should skip plan_010 since it's cancelled, but I need to account for the olmo_seed43 situation—it's currently analyzing rather than planned, yet it's central to the worst-case seed sensitivity narrative. I need to stick to what's actually in the experiment_plan with \"planned\" or \"RUNNING\" status rather than including registry items that aren't part of the original plan. So that gives me plan_014 through plan_026, plus the theoretical analysis section—those are the ones I should focus on.\n\nThough olmo_seed43 keeps coming up in the worst-tier metrics, it's not formally in the experiment_plan, so I'll mention it as supplementary context rather than a primary entry. Now I'm ready to write out the detailed YAML with worst-case scenarios for each planned experiment, starting with the 14B scale validation.\n\nFor the 14B model, LoRA fine-tuning only adjusts a tiny fraction of parameters, so the much larger capacity means recursive adjustments create minimal distributional shifts across depths—the model essentially absorbs the training signal without dramatic generation changes. This makes p90_ppl and var_surprisal far less diagnostic since the tail distribution stays robust, leaving 4-class accuracy around 52% and d1v2 AUC near 0.62 with only marginal feature overlap. The wild-data experiment then builds on this weak 14B signal to test calibration at scale.\n\nWith weak 14B signal, wild-data predictions become inconsistent across models, and C4 false positive rates shift dramatically depending on which reference model I use—there's no reliable evidence that recursive depth is actually detectable in real web corpora. Meanwhile, the detector baselines tell a different story: Binoculars and Fast-DetectGPT both capture ordinal signal from the synthetic-looking distributional shifts in deeper recursive text, reaching 63% and 58% accuracy respectively, and when I apply ordinal calibration Binoculars climbs to 65%—only 15 percentage points below the random forest and sometimes matching it in specific settings, which suggests specialized features might not be as necessary as I thought.\n\nThe bootstrap confidence intervals reveal just how noisy the weaker cells are, with widths of 6-8 percentage points in topk50 and some barely above chance at the 3-class level, plus another 1-3 percentage points of seed-to-seed variance on top. For the theory section, my EDD upper bound derivation gives 3 but empirical results show 4, the strategy-dependent convergence argument explains the temp09 reversal qualitatively but not quantitatively, and the tail erosion mechanism for p90_ppl is mechanically correct but doesn't yield novel predictions—reviewers are right that this reads more like post-hoc rationalization of known model collapse dynamics than actual theoretical contribution. On the API model front, GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning appears to suppress distributional shifts through its safety filters and RLHF regularization.\n\nThe depth signal in the API model is even weaker than in the 14B case, hitting only 35-40% on 4-class accuracy, and while the prompted recursive chain does show a depth signal, it's qualitatively different from what I see with LoRA fine-tuning—results don't transfer across these method types. For the theory section sketch, I'm connecting to Shumailov's work but not deriving anything new, the EDD bound still doesn't match the data, and reviewers are scoring it around 2.5-3.0 for theory quality.\n\nOrganizing this into YAML...\n\nI need to be careful about the seed experiments—they're in the registry but not explicitly in the experiment_plan, though olmo_seed43 shows up as a key factor in the worst tier definition. I think I should include it as a supplementary data point rather than forcing it into the planned experiments section. Let me focus the main imagined_experiments on what's actually in the plan: plan_014 for 14B validation, plan_015 for wild-data calibration, and plan_018.\n\nWriting the YAML structure now...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54649,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54649},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fc716cf-fd2e-40b7-99ed-5c56c1f4ef58","uuid":"a54da40c-4916-40fe-9a86-c3c43132e40e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016MVXeW2YKX4mRvmV6QFx8k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心叙事从\"depth estimation is feasible and robust\"收缩为\"characterizing the boundary conditions\n  of recursive depth signal\"。14B实验确认信号在主流规模下极弱（4-class acc ~52%，仅比instruct的47%高5pp），\n  与1B-scale的70-85%形成鲜明对比。理论section尝试用capacity-dependent attractor convergence解释这一差异，\n  但未产出可验证预测，审稿人视为retrospective rationalization。Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT ordinal baseline\n  达到63%，削弱specialized feature approach的必要性叙事。OLMo seed43 acc~72%（vs seed42的78.8%，Δ=6.8pp），\n  暴露seed sensitivity。论文重心移至：(a)task formalization仍成立，(b)Atlas揭示scale×strategy×architecture\n  三维交互（1B强/14B弱/instruct弱=完整picture），(c)负面结果的系统性价值。仍冲EMNLP Main \"New Missions\" track，\n  reviewer avg预期2.5-3.0。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"14B_scale_validation_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA, nucleus p=0.95, d0-d3递归链, 19特征提取 + RF/LR分类\"\n    expected_results:\n      rf_4class_acc: 0.52\n      rf_4class_ci: [0.505, 0.535]\n      lr_4class_acc: 0.47\n      rf_3class_acc: 0.42\n      auc_d0v1: 0.88\n      auc_d1v2: 0.62\n      auc_d1v3: 0.78\n      auc_d2v3: 0.58\n      edd_at_075: 1\n      edd_at_070: 1\n      top_features: [\"type_token_ratio\", \"p90_ppl\", \"rep_3gram\", \"surprisal_range\"]\n      feature_top4_overlap_with_1b: 1\n      finetune_loss_d1: 2.48\n      finetune_loss_d2: 2.31\n      finetune_loss_d3: 2.22\n      delta_vs_1b_best: -0.334\n      delta_vs_instruct: +0.046\n    result_rationale: >\n      14B模型有10倍于1.4B的参数量，LoRA仅调整~0.15%参数。递归fine-tuning对整体生成分布的扰动极小——\n      finetune loss从d0到d1仅下降~0.17（vs 1B的~0.6-0.9），说明模型容量足以在不大幅改变distributional\n      characteristics的情况下拟合下一深度数据。p90_ppl和var_surprisal在1B有效是因为小模型在递归fine-tuning\n      中快速丢失tail distribution（Shumailov tail erosion），但14B的更大表达能力延缓了这一过程，\n      adjacent depth之间的统计特征差异被压缩到noise level。d0v1仍可分（0.88）因为human vs 1st-gen\n      差异不依赖递归collapse，而是LoRA适配本身的distributional shift。但d1v2 AUC仅0.62，d2v3 0.58，\n      相邻深度几乎不可区分。feature ranking显著不同——type_token_ratio升至top1（因为14B在递归中\n      词汇多样性下降比perplexity shift更先出现），与1B的perplexity-dominated pattern仅1个重叠。\n      EDD=1意味着仅binary（d0 vs d1+）有意义，ordinal estimation在14B上实质失败。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 14B vs 1B scale comparison (4-class acc, d1v2 AUC, feature overlap)\"\n      - \"Table: 14B per-class recall (d0 ~90%, d1 ~45%, d2 ~30%, d3 ~40%)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC decay curve: 14B curve平坦且快速跌破threshold，vs 1B的缓慢衰减\"\n    analysis: >\n      52%的4-class acc仅比instruct model（47.4%）高4.6pp，比random chance（25%）高27pp。\n      审稿人会总结为\"depth signal exists but is practically negligible at 14B\"。\n      d0v1=0.88说明binary detection仍work，但这不是本文的contribution（已有大量binary detector）。\n      Feature ranking divergence（overlap 1/4）进一步说明1B发现的\"perplexity tail universality\"\n      不能推广到14B，是scale-specific phenomenon。论文必须将此定位为central finding而非limitation：\n      \"depth signal exhibits scale-dependent decay, with 14B confirming the theoretical\n      prediction that higher capacity delays distributional collapse\"。但这个claim需要\n      theory section支撑，而theory section本身在worst档被视为post-hoc。\n\n  - name: \"wild_data_calibration_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"C4/FineWeb/RedPajama子集，用3个已训练reference model提取19特征，3×3 RF分类器做depth预测+分布分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      c4_cross_model_d0_agreement: 0.61\n      c4_cross_model_d1plus_agreement: 0.23\n      fineweb_cross_model_d0_agreement: 0.68\n      fineweb_cross_model_d1plus_agreement: 0.19\n      redpajama_d0_pct_pythia: 0.72\n      redpajama_d0_pct_olmo: 0.91\n      redpajama_d0_pct_gpt2xl: 0.69\n      cross_model_kappa: 0.31\n      fpr_range_across_models: [4.7, 34.0]\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有实验显示wild data FPR在不同reference model间差异巨大（OLMo C4 FPR=4.7% vs Pythia=20.2%\n      vs GPT-2 XL=22.4%）。3-model ensemble的cross-model agreement在d0上reasonable（~65%），\n      但在d1+上极低（~20%），因为不同reference model的decision boundary位于feature space的不同位置。\n      RedPajama结果会进一步放大这一不一致性，因为其内容多样性（代码、书籍、Common Crawl混合）\n      比C4/FineWeb更heterogeneous。Cohen's kappa ~0.31表示fair agreement，远未达到\n      \"reliable depth estimation in the wild\"的标准。审稿人会指出：如果三个reference model\n      对同一文本的depth预测不一致，那么depth estimation的\"practical relevance\"存疑。\n      论文需诚实报告cross-model consistency低，定位为\"future work需要reference-model-invariant\n      features或ensemble calibration\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-model depth prediction agreement matrix (C4/FineWeb/RedPajama × 3 reference models)\"\n      - \"Table: Per-model FPR comparison across 3 web corpora\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: cross-model agreement rate by predicted depth class\"\n    analysis: >\n      野生数据校准在worst档下暴露了方法的fundamental deployment gap：在controlled setting中\n      reference model choice对acc影响仅~4pp（ref_model_ablation_001），但在wild data中\n      因为没有ground truth depth label，cross-model disagreement直接变成uncertainty。\n      FPR从4.7%到34%的range使得任何single-model depth prediction都不可信。\n      这与14B信号弱共同构成\"practical relevance unclear\"的审稿人总结。\n      论文应将此定位为\"open challenge\"而非failure，但不能claim wild data applicability。\n\n  - name: \"detector_ordinal_baseline_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT连续分数校准为ordinal depth bins, 在3×3已有数据上评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      binoculars_4class_acc: 0.63\n      binoculars_4class_ci: [0.615, 0.645]\n      binoculars_d1v2_auc: 0.72\n      binoculars_d2v3_auc: 0.65\n      binoculars_3class_acc: 0.55\n      fastdetectgpt_4class_acc: 0.58\n      fastdetectgpt_d1v2_auc: 0.68\n      fastdetectgpt_d2v3_auc: 0.61\n      binoculars_coral_4class_acc: 0.65\n      fastdetectgpt_coral_4class_acc: 0.60\n      rf_19feat_baseline: 0.783\n      delta_binoculars_vs_rf: -0.153\n      delta_fastdetectgpt_vs_rf: -0.203\n      binoculars_per_strategy:\n        nucleus: 0.67\n        temp09: 0.64\n        topk50: 0.58\n      binoculars_best_cell_acc: 0.71\n      binoculars_worst_cell_acc: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binoculars和Fast-DetectGPT的连续分数本质上捕捉了text的\"synthetic-ness\"程度，\n      而递归深度越大text越\"synthetic\"，所以这些分数天然具有与depth的单调相关性。\n      在worst档下，Binoculars利用cross-entropy和perplexity ratio的连续值，\n      通过CORAL ordinal regression校准后可达65%——这比RF的78.3%低13pp，\n      但比chance（25%）高40pp，比instruct model结果（47%）高18pp。\n      关键问题是在部分weak cells（topk50）上，Binoculars（58%）接近或超过RF（69.6%，\n      topk50 worst cell），gap缩小到<12pp。Fast-DetectGPT稍弱因为其perturbation-based\n      approach对ordinal gradient不如Binoculars的direct score sensitive。\n      审稿人看到63%的baseline后会质疑：19个手工特征+RF相比现成detector仅提升15pp，\n      是否justify了额外的complexity？这削弱了\"task需要specialized approach\"的叙事，\n      使论文更像\"incremental improvement over existing detectors\"而非\"new task formalization\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Detector ordinal baseline vs RF/CORAL/DivEye across 9 cells\"\n      - \"Table: Binoculars per-strategy breakdown showing gap varies by strategy\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: RF vs Binoculars vs Fast-DetectGPT per cell, showing gap shrinks in weak cells\"\n    analysis: >\n      63%的Binoculars baseline是worst档最具杀伤力的结果之一。它不会摧毁论文（RF仍consistently优15pp+），\n      但它将审稿人的framing从\"new capability enabled by our approach\"转向\"marginal improvement\n      over repurposed existing tools\"。论文需要argue：(a)这15pp在depth 1-3区分上更大\n      （Binoculars的3-class仅55% vs RF的72%），(b) Binoculars的ordinal signal来自binary\n      synthetic-ness的monotonic proxy而非genuine depth features，(c) RF的feature importance\n      analysis提供interpretability that Binoculars black-box score cannot。\n      但审稿人可能不买账——\"interpretability is a soft argument\"。\n\n  - name: \"bootstrap_ci_table1_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"从5-fold CV结果计算bootstrap CI for all 9 cells + cross-model/cross-strategy\"\n    expected_results:\n      mean_ci_width_4class: 3.2\n      max_ci_width_4class: 5.8\n      min_ci_width_4class: 1.4\n      topk50_cells_ci_width_avg: 4.9\n      temp09_cells_ci_width_avg: 2.8\n      nucleus_cells_ci_width_avg: 2.3\n      pythia_topk50_ci: [0.668, 0.726]\n      gpt2xl_temp09_ci: [0.838, 0.872]\n      overlap_count_adjacent_cells: 4\n      cross_model_loo_ci_width: 4.5\n      cross_strategy_loo_ci_width: 6.2\n      seed42_vs_seed43_ci_overlap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CI宽度反映CV fold间的variance。weak cells（topk50系列，acc ~69-75%）\n      的CI宽度会达到5-6pp，因为topk50的depth signal较弱导致不同fold间的分类边界不稳定。\n      strong cells（gpt2xl_temp09, 85.4%）CI窄（~2pp）因为信号强。关键问题是adjacent cells\n      之间存在CI overlap——例如Pythia nucleus（78.2%±2.5%）和Pythia temp09（76.2%±2.8%）\n      的CI重叠，意味着strategy effect在Pythia上不显著。cross-strategy LOO的CI最宽（~6pp），\n      因为holdout strategy的shift增大了fold variance。seed42 vs seed43的CI overlap\n      证实seed effect与model/strategy effect处于同一量级（especially OLMo），\n      审稿人会质疑reported differences的statistical significance。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 1 augmented: 9-cell matrix with bootstrap 95% CI\"\n      - \"Table: CI overlap matrix between adjacent cells\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: all 9 cells with CI error bars, sorted by accuracy\"\n    analysis: >\n      CI分析本身是methodologically sound且审稿人期望的。问题在于worst档下CI揭示的high variance\n      削弱了precise claims的可信度。论文不能再写\"topk50 achieves 69.6%\"而要写\"69.6% [66.8%, 72.6%]\"，\n      下界66.8%仅比Binoculars baseline（63%）高3.8pp，统计显著性存疑。\n      cross-model LOO的CI宽度进一步限制了generalization claims。\n\n  - name: \"theoretical_analysis_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"连接depth signal到model collapse理论: tail erosion mechanism, EDD上界推导, strategy-dependent convergence\"\n    expected_results:\n      tail_erosion_mechanism: \"qualitative_match\"\n      edd_upper_bound_derived: 6\n      edd_empirical: 4\n      edd_bound_gap: 2\n      testable_prediction_count: 0\n      strategy_convergence_quantitative: false\n      scale_decay_prediction: \"qualitative_only\"\n      reviewer_assessment: \"retrospective_rationalization\"\n      section_length_pages: 0.75\n      new_theorems: 0\n      new_lemmas: 0\n      empirical_validation_points: 3\n      validation_pass_rate: 0.33\n    result_rationale: >\n      Theory section尝试三件事：(1) 用Shumailov tail erosion解释p90_ppl/var_surprisal为何dominant——\n      这是正确的但trivially follows from existing theory，不是新贡献。(2) 从Dohmatob contraction\n      rates推导EDD上界——推导出EDD≤6，但empirical EDD=4，bound太松（gap=2），审稿人会说\n      \"a bound that doesn't bind is not a contribution\"。(3) 解释strategy-dependent convergence——\n      temperature的uniform logit scaling加速收敛是qualitative argument，无法quantify\n      多快或预测具体AUC值。三个validation points中只有tail erosion mechanism match（1/3），\n      EDD bound不紧，strategy convergence rate无quantitative prediction。\n      审稿人评价：\"This section retroactively explains known model collapse dynamics\n      using established theoretical frameworks. While the connections are reasonable,\n      no new theoretical results are derived and no falsifiable predictions are made.\n      The EDD bound (≤6 vs empirical 4) is too loose to be informative.\"\n      这直接触发worst档核心假设之一。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Theoretical predictions vs empirical observations (3 rows, 1/3 match)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Diagram: theoretical attractor convergence framework (qualitative)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Theory section的根本问题是从empirical observations反推theoretical explanation，\n      而非从theory预测phenomena。即使explanation合理，审稿人区分explanatory power和predictive power。\n      在worst档下，theory section既不产出新theorem也不产出testable prediction，\n      仅提供narrative coherence。这对\"no method contribution\"的审稿concern没有帮助——\n      如果theory也不算contribution，论文就只剩task formalization + empirical atlas。\n      对于EMNLP Main来说，这需要atlas的发现足够novel和impactful来stand alone，\n      但14B弱信号和Binoculars baseline 63%共同削弱了impact argument。\n\n  - name: \"api_model_recursive_chains_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_026\"\n    description: \"GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API递归链 + prompted recursive chain (rewrite/continue)\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4omini_ft_4class_acc: 0.38\n      gpt4omini_ft_d1v2_auc: 0.55\n      gpt4omini_ft_d0v1_auc: 0.75\n      prompted_rewrite_4class_acc: 0.33\n      prompted_rewrite_d1v2_auc: 0.52\n      feature_overlap_with_lora: 0\n      cross_method_transfer_acc: 0.27\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o-mini的fine-tuning API限制（固定epochs、受限learning rate、safety guardrails）\n      使得递归fine-tuning的distributional shift远小于本地LoRA。模型的RLHF对齐和safety training\n      作为implicit regularizer抑制了generation distribution的drift——即使fine-tune到depth 3，\n      输出仍被RLHF拉回safety-aligned distribution。4-class acc 38%仅略高于chance（25%），\n      d1v2 AUC 0.55接近random。Prompted rewrite chain更差（33%），因为\"rewrite this text\"\n      的prompt不产生与LoRA fine-tuning相同的distributional shift——rewrite是content-level\n      transformation而非distribution-level collapse。Feature overlap为0说明API model\n      depth signal（如果存在）的statistical signature完全不同于LoRA-induced signal。\n      cross-method transfer（用LoRA训练的RF预测API model depth）仅27%≈chance，\n      确认两种method产生的\"depth\"是fundamentally different phenomena。\n      审稿人总结：\"depth signal is specific to the LoRA fine-tuning mechanism,\n      not a general property of recursive generation\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: API model vs LoRA model depth estimation comparison\"\n      - \"Table: Cross-method transfer matrix\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Feature trajectory comparison: API vs LoRA models across depths\"\n    analysis: >\n      API model结果在worst档下是devastating：它直接支持审稿人的\"phenomenon specific to\n      small base models with LoRA fine-tuning\"总结。如果depth signal仅在特定fine-tuning\n      mechanism下存在且不迁移到commercial API models，practical relevance严重受限。\n      论文只能将此定位为\"important negative result that constrains the scope of depth estimation\"\n      并诚实acknowledge \"our framework applies to LoRA-based recursive generation,\n      the dominant paradigm in current model collapse studies (Shumailov, Drayson),\n      but extending to API-based or prompt-based recursion remains open\"。\n      这进一步收缩了contribution scope。\n\n  - name: \"theory_section_whatif_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"what_if:theory_section\"\n    description: \"半页理论sketch: tail erosion → p90_ppl, EDD上界 from contraction rates, strategy convergence\"\n    expected_results:\n      section_quality_score: 2.0\n      reviewer_1_comment: \"post-hoc rationalization of known dynamics\"\n      reviewer_2_comment: \"no novel theoretical results, EDD bound vacuous\"\n      reviewer_3_comment: \"the theoretical framing is reasonable but doesn't rise to the level of a contribution\"\n      contribution_upgrade: false\n      addresses_no_method_concern: false\n      strengthens_atlas_narrative: \"marginally\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      What-if theory section在worst档的效果是marginal而非transformative。三位审稿人中\n      两位直接否定其contribution status。根本原因：(1) Shumailov/Dohmatob/Gerstgrasser\n      已建立了model collapse理论框架，我们的theory section仅应用这些已知框架到depth estimation\n      设定，不产出新理论。(2) EDD bound太松（≤6 vs empirical 4），说明理论分析的precision\n      不足以指导实验设计或预测结果。(3) strategy convergence explanation是qualitative analogy\n      而非formal derivation。在worst档审稿人看来，theory section占0.75页版面但不增加\n      信息量——读者从empirical results table已能得出相同结论。\n      theory section不能解决\"no method contribution\"问题，因为理论分析和方法贡献是\n      正交维度——审稿人想看的是novel algorithm/architecture/loss，不是对已知现象的理论解释。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Theory section在worst档是net neutral to slightly negative——它不伤害论文，\n      但占用了宝贵版面（0.75页）却不升级任何claim的strength。更好的利用方式可能是\n      用这0.75页扩展Atlas analysis或添加更多ablation。但如果不放theory section，\n      审稿人又会说\"no theoretical grounding\"。这是worst档的catch-22：放了被批post-hoc，\n      不放被批no theory。建议保留但压缩到0.5页，降低期望为\"theoretical context\"而非\"contribution\"。\n\n  - name: \"olmo_seed43_supplementary_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"registry:olmo_seed43_001\"\n    description: \"OLMo-1B seed43递归链, 验证seed robustness（补充experiment_plan外的关键worst档指标）\"\n    expected_results:\n      rf_4class_acc: 0.72\n      rf_4class_ci: [0.708, 0.732]\n      d1v2_auc: 0.79\n      delta_vs_seed42: -0.068\n      delta_vs_seed42_pp: -6.8\n      per_class_recall:\n        d0: 0.97\n        d1: 0.76\n        d2: 0.48\n        d3: 0.67\n      top_features: [\"p90_ppl\", \"var_surprisal\", \"mean_ppl\", \"p75_ppl\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      cross_seed_max_delta_all_models: 6.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      OLMo-1B在seed42下是3×3矩阵中表现中等的模型（78.8%），但seed43在worst档下暴露\n      显著sensitivity。Δ=6.8pp远超GPT-2 XL（Δ=2.0pp）和Pythia（Δ=0.6pp）。\n      根本原因是OLMo-1B的Dolma训练数据和模型架构使其对LoRA初始化seed更敏感——\n      不同seed下LoRA权重收敛到不同local minima，产生不同的generation distribution shift。\n      seed43的d2 recall仅48%（vs seed42的60.7%），说明depth 2是最不稳定的分类边界。\n      6.8pp的max delta迫使论文加入variance analysis section，承认\"reported accuracies\n      have seed-dependent variance of up to 6.8pp for OLMo, requiring multi-seed\n      averaging for reliable conclusions\"。审稿人会用这个数据argue论文的所有point estimates\n      都需要±3-4pp的implicit error bar，使得许多marginal claims不再显著。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-seed comparison (3 models × 2 seeds)\"\n      - \"Table: Per-class recall variance across seeds\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Error bar plot: seed42 vs seed43 accuracy with CIs for all 3 models\"\n    analysis: >\n      6.8pp的seed sensitivity是worst档中第二具杀伤力的结果（仅次于14B弱信号）。\n      它不仅影响OLMo自身的结果可信度，还cast doubt on整个3×3矩阵中仅跑了1个seed的其他cells。\n      Pythia seed delta仅0.6pp说明seed sensitivity是model-dependent的，\n      但审稿人会argue \"without multi-seed results for all cells, we cannot know\n      which other cells have OLMo-like sensitivity\"。论文必须加入variance analysis section\n      （worst档核心假设之一），报告已有的3-model 2-seed results，并在limitations中\n      明确承认seed sensitivity as a systematic uncertainty。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54649,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54649},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fc716cf-fd2e-40b7-99ed-5c56c1f4ef58","uuid":"36d52e3d-4522-4f14-8190-bbf2901fabc7"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":234227,"duration_api_ms":236617,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心叙事从\"depth estimation is feasible and robust\"收缩为\"characterizing the boundary conditions\n  of recursive depth signal\"。14B实验确认信号在主流规模下极弱（4-class acc ~52%，仅比instruct的47%高5pp），\n  与1B-scale的70-85%形成鲜明对比。理论section尝试用capacity-dependent attractor convergence解释这一差异，\n  但未产出可验证预测，审稿人视为retrospective rationalization。Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT ordinal baseline\n  达到63%，削弱specialized feature approach的必要性叙事。OLMo seed43 acc~72%（vs seed42的78.8%，Δ=6.8pp），\n  暴露seed sensitivity。论文重心移至：(a)task formalization仍成立，(b)Atlas揭示scale×strategy×architecture\n  三维交互（1B强/14B弱/instruct弱=完整picture），(c)负面结果的系统性价值。仍冲EMNLP Main \"New Missions\" track，\n  reviewer avg预期2.5-3.0。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"14B_scale_validation_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA, nucleus p=0.95, d0-d3递归链, 19特征提取 + RF/LR分类\"\n    expected_results:\n      rf_4class_acc: 0.52\n      rf_4class_ci: [0.505, 0.535]\n      lr_4class_acc: 0.47\n      rf_3class_acc: 0.42\n      auc_d0v1: 0.88\n      auc_d1v2: 0.62\n      auc_d1v3: 0.78\n      auc_d2v3: 0.58\n      edd_at_075: 1\n      edd_at_070: 1\n      top_features: [\"type_token_ratio\", \"p90_ppl\", \"rep_3gram\", \"surprisal_range\"]\n      feature_top4_overlap_with_1b: 1\n      finetune_loss_d1: 2.48\n      finetune_loss_d2: 2.31\n      finetune_loss_d3: 2.22\n      delta_vs_1b_best: -0.334\n      delta_vs_instruct: +0.046\n    result_rationale: >\n      14B模型有10倍于1.4B的参数量，LoRA仅调整~0.15%参数。递归fine-tuning对整体生成分布的扰动极小——\n      finetune loss从d0到d1仅下降~0.17（vs 1B的~0.6-0.9），说明模型容量足以在不大幅改变distributional\n      characteristics的情况下拟合下一深度数据。p90_ppl和var_surprisal在1B有效是因为小模型在递归fine-tuning\n      中快速丢失tail distribution（Shumailov tail erosion），但14B的更大表达能力延缓了这一过程，\n      adjacent depth之间的统计特征差异被压缩到noise level。d0v1仍可分（0.88）因为human vs 1st-gen\n      差异不依赖递归collapse，而是LoRA适配本身的distributional shift。但d1v2 AUC仅0.62，d2v3 0.58，\n      相邻深度几乎不可区分。feature ranking显著不同——type_token_ratio升至top1（因为14B在递归中\n      词汇多样性下降比perplexity shift更先出现），与1B的perplexity-dominated pattern仅1个重叠。\n      EDD=1意味着仅binary（d0 vs d1+）有意义，ordinal estimation在14B上实质失败。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 14B vs 1B scale comparison (4-class acc, d1v2 AUC, feature overlap)\"\n      - \"Table: 14B per-class recall (d0 ~90%, d1 ~45%, d2 ~30%, d3 ~40%)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC decay curve: 14B curve平坦且快速跌破threshold，vs 1B的缓慢衰减\"\n    analysis: >\n      52%的4-class acc仅比instruct model（47.4%）高4.6pp，比random chance（25%）高27pp。\n      审稿人会总结为\"depth signal exists but is practically negligible at 14B\"。\n      d0v1=0.88说明binary detection仍work，但这不是本文的contribution（已有大量binary detector）。\n      Feature ranking divergence（overlap 1/4）进一步说明1B发现的\"perplexity tail universality\"\n      不能推广到14B，是scale-specific phenomenon。论文必须将此定位为central finding而非limitation：\n      \"depth signal exhibits scale-dependent decay, with 14B confirming the theoretical\n      prediction that higher capacity delays distributional collapse\"。但这个claim需要\n      theory section支撑，而theory section本身在worst档被视为post-hoc。\n\n  - name: \"wild_data_calibration_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"C4/FineWeb/RedPajama子集，用3个已训练reference model提取19特征，3×3 RF分类器做depth预测+分布分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      c4_cross_model_d0_agreement: 0.61\n      c4_cross_model_d1plus_agreement: 0.23\n      fineweb_cross_model_d0_agreement: 0.68\n      fineweb_cross_model_d1plus_agreement: 0.19\n      redpajama_d0_pct_pythia: 0.72\n      redpajama_d0_pct_olmo: 0.91\n      redpajama_d0_pct_gpt2xl: 0.69\n      cross_model_kappa: 0.31\n      fpr_range_across_models: [4.7, 34.0]\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有实验显示wild data FPR在不同reference model间差异巨大（OLMo C4 FPR=4.7% vs Pythia=20.2%\n      vs GPT-2 XL=22.4%）。3-model ensemble的cross-model agreement在d0上reasonable（~65%），\n      但在d1+上极低（~20%），因为不同reference model的decision boundary位于feature space的不同位置。\n      RedPajama结果会进一步放大这一不一致性，因为其内容多样性（代码、书籍、Common Crawl混合）\n      比C4/FineWeb更heterogeneous。Cohen's kappa ~0.31表示fair agreement，远未达到\n      \"reliable depth estimation in the wild\"的标准。审稿人会指出：如果三个reference model\n      对同一文本的depth预测不一致，那么depth estimation的\"practical relevance\"存疑。\n      论文需诚实报告cross-model consistency低，定位为\"future work需要reference-model-invariant\n      features或ensemble calibration\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-model depth prediction agreement matrix (C4/FineWeb/RedPajama × 3 reference models)\"\n      - \"Table: Per-model FPR comparison across 3 web corpora\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: cross-model agreement rate by predicted depth class\"\n    analysis: >\n      野生数据校准在worst档下暴露了方法的fundamental deployment gap：在controlled setting中\n      reference model choice对acc影响仅~4pp（ref_model_ablation_001），但在wild data中\n      因为没有ground truth depth label，cross-model disagreement直接变成uncertainty。\n      FPR从4.7%到34%的range使得任何single-model depth prediction都不可信。\n      这与14B信号弱共同构成\"practical relevance unclear\"的审稿人总结。\n      论文应将此定位为\"open challenge\"而非failure，但不能claim wild data applicability。\n\n  - name: \"detector_ordinal_baseline_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT连续分数校准为ordinal depth bins, 在3×3已有数据上评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      binoculars_4class_acc: 0.63\n      binoculars_4class_ci: [0.615, 0.645]\n      binoculars_d1v2_auc: 0.72\n      binoculars_d2v3_auc: 0.65\n      binoculars_3class_acc: 0.55\n      fastdetectgpt_4class_acc: 0.58\n      fastdetectgpt_d1v2_auc: 0.68\n      fastdetectgpt_d2v3_auc: 0.61\n      binoculars_coral_4class_acc: 0.65\n      fastdetectgpt_coral_4class_acc: 0.60\n      rf_19feat_baseline: 0.783\n      delta_binoculars_vs_rf: -0.153\n      delta_fastdetectgpt_vs_rf: -0.203\n      binoculars_per_strategy:\n        nucleus: 0.67\n        temp09: 0.64\n        topk50: 0.58\n      binoculars_best_cell_acc: 0.71\n      binoculars_worst_cell_acc: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binoculars和Fast-DetectGPT的连续分数本质上捕捉了text的\"synthetic-ness\"程度，\n      而递归深度越大text越\"synthetic\"，所以这些分数天然具有与depth的单调相关性。\n      在worst档下，Binoculars利用cross-entropy和perplexity ratio的连续值，\n      通过CORAL ordinal regression校准后可达65%——这比RF的78.3%低13pp，\n      但比chance（25%）高40pp，比instruct model结果（47%）高18pp。\n      关键问题是在部分weak cells（topk50）上，Binoculars（58%）接近或超过RF（69.6%，\n      topk50 worst cell），gap缩小到<12pp。Fast-DetectGPT稍弱因为其perturbation-based\n      approach对ordinal gradient不如Binoculars的direct score sensitive。\n      审稿人看到63%的baseline后会质疑：19个手工特征+RF相比现成detector仅提升15pp，\n      是否justify了额外的complexity？这削弱了\"task需要specialized approach\"的叙事，\n      使论文更像\"incremental improvement over existing detectors\"而非\"new task formalization\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Detector ordinal baseline vs RF/CORAL/DivEye across 9 cells\"\n      - \"Table: Binoculars per-strategy breakdown showing gap varies by strategy\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: RF vs Binoculars vs Fast-DetectGPT per cell, showing gap shrinks in weak cells\"\n    analysis: >\n      63%的Binoculars baseline是worst档最具杀伤力的结果之一。它不会摧毁论文（RF仍consistently优15pp+），\n      但它将审稿人的framing从\"new capability enabled by our approach\"转向\"marginal improvement\n      over repurposed existing tools\"。论文需要argue：(a)这15pp在depth 1-3区分上更大\n      （Binoculars的3-class仅55% vs RF的72%），(b) Binoculars的ordinal signal来自binary\n      synthetic-ness的monotonic proxy而非genuine depth features，(c) RF的feature importance\n      analysis提供interpretability that Binoculars black-box score cannot。\n      但审稿人可能不买账——\"interpretability is a soft argument\"。\n\n  - name: \"bootstrap_ci_table1_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"从5-fold CV结果计算bootstrap CI for all 9 cells + cross-model/cross-strategy\"\n    expected_results:\n      mean_ci_width_4class: 3.2\n      max_ci_width_4class: 5.8\n      min_ci_width_4class: 1.4\n      topk50_cells_ci_width_avg: 4.9\n      temp09_cells_ci_width_avg: 2.8\n      nucleus_cells_ci_width_avg: 2.3\n      pythia_topk50_ci: [0.668, 0.726]\n      gpt2xl_temp09_ci: [0.838, 0.872]\n      overlap_count_adjacent_cells: 4\n      cross_model_loo_ci_width: 4.5\n      cross_strategy_loo_ci_width: 6.2\n      seed42_vs_seed43_ci_overlap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CI宽度反映CV fold间的variance。weak cells（topk50系列，acc ~69-75%）\n      的CI宽度会达到5-6pp，因为topk50的depth signal较弱导致不同fold间的分类边界不稳定。\n      strong cells（gpt2xl_temp09, 85.4%）CI窄（~2pp）因为信号强。关键问题是adjacent cells\n      之间存在CI overlap——例如Pythia nucleus（78.2%±2.5%）和Pythia temp09（76.2%±2.8%）\n      的CI重叠，意味着strategy effect在Pythia上不显著。cross-strategy LOO的CI最宽（~6pp），\n      因为holdout strategy的shift增大了fold variance。seed42 vs seed43的CI overlap\n      证实seed effect与model/strategy effect处于同一量级（especially OLMo），\n      审稿人会质疑reported differences的statistical significance。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 1 augmented: 9-cell matrix with bootstrap 95% CI\"\n      - \"Table: CI overlap matrix between adjacent cells\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: all 9 cells with CI error bars, sorted by accuracy\"\n    analysis: >\n      CI分析本身是methodologically sound且审稿人期望的。问题在于worst档下CI揭示的high variance\n      削弱了precise claims的可信度。论文不能再写\"topk50 achieves 69.6%\"而要写\"69.6% [66.8%, 72.6%]\"，\n      下界66.8%仅比Binoculars baseline（63%）高3.8pp，统计显著性存疑。\n      cross-model LOO的CI宽度进一步限制了generalization claims。\n\n  - name: \"theoretical_analysis_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"连接depth signal到model collapse理论: tail erosion mechanism, EDD上界推导, strategy-dependent convergence\"\n    expected_results:\n      tail_erosion_mechanism: \"qualitative_match\"\n      edd_upper_bound_derived: 6\n      edd_empirical: 4\n      edd_bound_gap: 2\n      testable_prediction_count: 0\n      strategy_convergence_quantitative: false\n      scale_decay_prediction: \"qualitative_only\"\n      reviewer_assessment: \"retrospective_rationalization\"\n      section_length_pages: 0.75\n      new_theorems: 0\n      new_lemmas: 0\n      empirical_validation_points: 3\n      validation_pass_rate: 0.33\n    result_rationale: >\n      Theory section尝试三件事：(1) 用Shumailov tail erosion解释p90_ppl/var_surprisal为何dominant——\n      这是正确的但trivially follows from existing theory，不是新贡献。(2) 从Dohmatob contraction\n      rates推导EDD上界——推导出EDD≤6，但empirical EDD=4，bound太松（gap=2），审稿人会说\n      \"a bound that doesn't bind is not a contribution\"。(3) 解释strategy-dependent convergence——\n      temperature的uniform logit scaling加速收敛是qualitative argument，无法quantify\n      多快或预测具体AUC值。三个validation points中只有tail erosion mechanism match（1/3），\n      EDD bound不紧，strategy convergence rate无quantitative prediction。\n      审稿人评价：\"This section retroactively explains known model collapse dynamics\n      using established theoretical frameworks. While the connections are reasonable,\n      no new theoretical results are derived and no falsifiable predictions are made.\n      The EDD bound (≤6 vs empirical 4) is too loose to be informative.\"\n      这直接触发worst档核心假设之一。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Theoretical predictions vs empirical observations (3 rows, 1/3 match)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Diagram: theoretical attractor convergence framework (qualitative)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Theory section的根本问题是从empirical observations反推theoretical explanation，\n      而非从theory预测phenomena。即使explanation合理，审稿人区分explanatory power和predictive power。\n      在worst档下，theory section既不产出新theorem也不产出testable prediction，\n      仅提供narrative coherence。这对\"no method contribution\"的审稿concern没有帮助——\n      如果theory也不算contribution，论文就只剩task formalization + empirical atlas。\n      对于EMNLP Main来说，这需要atlas的发现足够novel和impactful来stand alone，\n      但14B弱信号和Binoculars baseline 63%共同削弱了impact argument。\n\n  - name: \"api_model_recursive_chains_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_026\"\n    description: \"GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API递归链 + prompted recursive chain (rewrite/continue)\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4omini_ft_4class_acc: 0.38\n      gpt4omini_ft_d1v2_auc: 0.55\n      gpt4omini_ft_d0v1_auc: 0.75\n      prompted_rewrite_4class_acc: 0.33\n      prompted_rewrite_d1v2_auc: 0.52\n      feature_overlap_with_lora: 0\n      cross_method_transfer_acc: 0.27\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o-mini的fine-tuning API限制（固定epochs、受限learning rate、safety guardrails）\n      使得递归fine-tuning的distributional shift远小于本地LoRA。模型的RLHF对齐和safety training\n      作为implicit regularizer抑制了generation distribution的drift——即使fine-tune到depth 3，\n      输出仍被RLHF拉回safety-aligned distribution。4-class acc 38%仅略高于chance（25%），\n      d1v2 AUC 0.55接近random。Prompted rewrite chain更差（33%），因为\"rewrite this text\"\n      的prompt不产生与LoRA fine-tuning相同的distributional shift——rewrite是content-level\n      transformation而非distribution-level collapse。Feature overlap为0说明API model\n      depth signal（如果存在）的statistical signature完全不同于LoRA-induced signal。\n      cross-method transfer（用LoRA训练的RF预测API model depth）仅27%≈chance，\n      确认两种method产生的\"depth\"是fundamentally different phenomena。\n      审稿人总结：\"depth signal is specific to the LoRA fine-tuning mechanism,\n      not a general property of recursive generation\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: API model vs LoRA model depth estimation comparison\"\n      - \"Table: Cross-method transfer matrix\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Feature trajectory comparison: API vs LoRA models across depths\"\n    analysis: >\n      API model结果在worst档下是devastating：它直接支持审稿人的\"phenomenon specific to\n      small base models with LoRA fine-tuning\"总结。如果depth signal仅在特定fine-tuning\n      mechanism下存在且不迁移到commercial API models，practical relevance严重受限。\n      论文只能将此定位为\"important negative result that constrains the scope of depth estimation\"\n      并诚实acknowledge \"our framework applies to LoRA-based recursive generation,\n      the dominant paradigm in current model collapse studies (Shumailov, Drayson),\n      but extending to API-based or prompt-based recursion remains open\"。\n      这进一步收缩了contribution scope。\n\n  - name: \"theory_section_whatif_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"what_if:theory_section\"\n    description: \"半页理论sketch: tail erosion → p90_ppl, EDD上界 from contraction rates, strategy convergence\"\n    expected_results:\n      section_quality_score: 2.0\n      reviewer_1_comment: \"post-hoc rationalization of known dynamics\"\n      reviewer_2_comment: \"no novel theoretical results, EDD bound vacuous\"\n      reviewer_3_comment: \"the theoretical framing is reasonable but doesn't rise to the level of a contribution\"\n      contribution_upgrade: false\n      addresses_no_method_concern: false\n      strengthens_atlas_narrative: \"marginally\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      What-if theory section在worst档的效果是marginal而非transformative。三位审稿人中\n      两位直接否定其contribution status。根本原因：(1) Shumailov/Dohmatob/Gerstgrasser\n      已建立了model collapse理论框架，我们的theory section仅应用这些已知框架到depth estimation\n      设定，不产出新理论。(2) EDD bound太松（≤6 vs empirical 4），说明理论分析的precision\n      不足以指导实验设计或预测结果。(3) strategy convergence explanation是qualitative analogy\n      而非formal derivation。在worst档审稿人看来，theory section占0.75页版面但不增加\n      信息量——读者从empirical results table已能得出相同结论。\n      theory section不能解决\"no method contribution\"问题，因为理论分析和方法贡献是\n      正交维度——审稿人想看的是novel algorithm/architecture/loss，不是对已知现象的理论解释。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Theory section在worst档是net neutral to slightly negative——它不伤害论文，\n      但占用了宝贵版面（0.75页）却不升级任何claim的strength。更好的利用方式可能是\n      用这0.75页扩展Atlas analysis或添加更多ablation。但如果不放theory section，\n      审稿人又会说\"no theoretical grounding\"。这是worst档的catch-22：放了被批post-hoc，\n      不放被批no theory。建议保留但压缩到0.5页，降低期望为\"theoretical context\"而非\"contribution\"。\n\n  - name: \"olmo_seed43_supplementary_worst\"\n    plan_id: \"registry:olmo_seed43_001\"\n    description: \"OLMo-1B seed43递归链, 验证seed robustness（补充experiment_plan外的关键worst档指标）\"\n    expected_results:\n      rf_4class_acc: 0.72\n      rf_4class_ci: [0.708, 0.732]\n      d1v2_auc: 0.79\n      delta_vs_seed42: -0.068\n      delta_vs_seed42_pp: -6.8\n      per_class_recall:\n        d0: 0.97\n        d1: 0.76\n        d2: 0.48\n        d3: 0.67\n      top_features: [\"p90_ppl\", \"var_surprisal\", \"mean_ppl\", \"p75_ppl\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      cross_seed_max_delta_all_models: 6.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      OLMo-1B在seed42下是3×3矩阵中表现中等的模型（78.8%），但seed43在worst档下暴露\n      显著sensitivity。Δ=6.8pp远超GPT-2 XL（Δ=2.0pp）和Pythia（Δ=0.6pp）。\n      根本原因是OLMo-1B的Dolma训练数据和模型架构使其对LoRA初始化seed更敏感——\n      不同seed下LoRA权重收敛到不同local minima，产生不同的generation distribution shift。\n      seed43的d2 recall仅48%（vs seed42的60.7%），说明depth 2是最不稳定的分类边界。\n      6.8pp的max delta迫使论文加入variance analysis section，承认\"reported accuracies\n      have seed-dependent variance of up to 6.8pp for OLMo, requiring multi-seed\n      averaging for reliable conclusions\"。审稿人会用这个数据argue论文的所有point estimates\n      都需要±3-4pp的implicit error bar，使得许多marginal claims不再显著。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-seed comparison (3 models × 2 seeds)\"\n      - \"Table: Per-class recall variance across seeds\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Error bar plot: seed42 vs seed43 accuracy with CIs for all 3 models\"\n    analysis: >\n      6.8pp的seed sensitivity是worst档中第二具杀伤力的结果（仅次于14B弱信号）。\n      它不仅影响OLMo自身的结果可信度，还cast doubt on整个3×3矩阵中仅跑了1个seed的其他cells。\n      Pythia seed delta仅0.6pp说明seed sensitivity是model-dependent的，\n      但审稿人会argue \"without multi-seed results for all cells, we cannot know\n      which other cells have OLMo-like sensitivity\"。论文必须加入variance analysis section\n      （worst档核心假设之一），报告已有的3-model 2-seed results，并在limitations中\n      明确承认seed sensitivity as a systematic uncertainty。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6fc716cf-fd2e-40b7-99ed-5c56c1f4ef58","total_cost_usd":0.6620287499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54649,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":10594,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54649,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10594,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54649},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":49612,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.049692,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10594,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":54649,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.61233675,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"3d984854-be2a-4bf9-b611-45194a42b433"}
